From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:51:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/30] S2: decode step timeline behind G6_S2_TIMELINE=N

Every rank, off by default. Around each decode step launch (main,
first-form draft, chain, DFlash2 context-only and query steps) the host
stamps its clock and records a CUDA event before and after the graph
launch; after the fence it adds the step's GPU span, input prep, launch
call and fence wait to per-kind totals, and the GPU idle since the
previous step's end event plus the host time since the previous fence to
per-transition totals. Printed every N main steps. Prefill quanta, mode
switches and the drafter's prompt fill cut the chain; gaps over 20 ms
count as breaks. Sizes the host round trip that a device-side accept and
launch could remove.
---
 engine/runtime/g6m4.cu       | 11 ++++-
 engine/runtime/s2/native.cuh | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 frontend/README.md           |  2 +
 3 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

